Pumpkin Swirl Brownies
  --Bianca Dodson

1 c unsalted butter -melted
1 c sugar
1 tsp vanilla
3 eggs
1 teaspoon Baking Powder
1/2 tsp salt
1 c ap flour
1 tsp pumpkin pie spice
1/2 c cocoa powder
1 c pumpkin puree

Preheat the oven to 350F. In a medium bowl mix together melted butter, sugar, and vanilla. Once combined, add in eggs one at a time. Add the flour, pumpkin pie spice, baking powder, and salt to the bowl and mix until well combined. Separate half the batter into a separate bowl, add cocoa powder and mix until completely combined. In the other bowl, add pumpkin puree and mix until well combined. Spray a 8x8" cake pan with nonstick baking spray. Add both the chocolate and pumpkin batter, alternating between the two. Bake for 20-25 min or until toothpick comes out clean.
